    "result_text": "Everything is consistent \u2014 and notably, only the hsqldb dialect used positional (column-less) INSERTs, so it was the only one that broke; h2/postgres use explicit column lists and, like the pre-existing `namesake_count`, don't list it in their schema files (they rely on `ddl-auto`). So no further files need touching.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is implemented and the suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\nI followed the existing `namesakeCount` convention exactly \u2014 a persisted, read-only owner field populated by a small pipeline step and auto-mapped to the DTO \u2014 so the value survives the create and is read back on `GET /api/owners/{id}` as the test requires.\n\nFiles touched:\n- **`FlagBulkSignup.java`** (new) \u2014 a single cohesive function mirroring `CountNamesakes`/`EnsureDailyLimit`: counts owners already created today and sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`. New class \u2192 zero surrounding complexity.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted one `flagBulkSignup` step between `ensureDailyLimit` and `save` (so the flag is set before persistence).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` field plus a plain getter/setter (each CC 1).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it.\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column and a trailing `NULL` to the ten positional seed INSERTs (that dialect's inserts are column-less; the h2/postgres dialects use explicit column lists and, like `namesake_count`, needed no change).\n\nI kept every changed function trivial (CC 1) and added the behaviour as an isolated new step rather than growing `EnsureDailyLimit` or the responder, so no large-class method was modified beyond the unavoidable field accessors.",
